  "description": "Currently, TPC-H and TPC-DS answer files (~4.2 MB total) are only available in\nsource distributions, not in wheels. When running from an installed wheel,\nvalidation is gracefully skipped with an INFO message.\n\nThis TODO implements Option C from the wheel packaging analysis: download\nanswer files on-demand from a CDN or GitHub releases, caching them locally\nfor subsequent runs.\n\nBenefits:\n- Zero wheel size impact (currently 7.1 MB, would be 11.3 MB with answers)\n- Validation available for all installation methods\n- Lazy loading - only downloads when validation is actually needed\n- Cache invalidation possible for answer file updates\n\nCurrent state (acceptable workaround):\n- Commit be3843c9 caches FileNotFoundError to prevent repeated warnings\n- Users see single INFO message: \"Validation will be skipped\"\n- This TODO is enhancement, not critical fix",
